A||||1||86_Fastback||Wheel bearings
Z||000000||86_Fastback||04-15-99||11:26 AM||||I am planning on replacing the front wheel bearings this weekend and I would like to know how difficult it is. I have not done this myself before. What parts do I need besides inner bearings, outer bearings and the seal? Any special tools and/or instructions for me? Thanks for every ones help.<br>Gregg
Z||000001||theogre||04-15-99||07:32 PM||||If you've never done this type work before, I'd recomend getting a a book for the car.<p>there are no special tools, but the book gives you the torq spec, if there is one, and other information.<p>if you do this without a torq wrench, like most people do..... hold the wrench near the nut, Not the far end, when tightening the spindle nut. tighten the nut untill the major slop is gone. then spin the wheel, and tighten untill snug. losen the nut a bit, then tighten till snug again. Spin the wheel a bit both times when tightening.<p>If the bearings are too lose, or too tight, you WILL fry them in very short order.<p>Before replaceing the bearings, also inspect the outer racees VERY thouroghly. If there is any outer race damage they must be replaced. (You may have to replace the hub. I'm not sure the races are available.)
